title start
kind: note
tags: business-plan conventions folder-naming-pattern
Conventions folder naming pattern
title end

paragraph start
An area folder is a two digit number followed by a full description of what the area covers. A subfolder is a number, the area key and the subject of the subfolder.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The tree has three levels at most: area, subfolder and file. A deeper level is added only when a subfolder grows past one clear subject.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Every folder holds a purpose file, named zero zero, then the folder name, then purpose and plan. An area that handles equipment ends with a hardware folder, and every area ends with an ai and automation folder.
paragraph end

